            <div xml:id="d619">

                <pb facs="0597" n="587" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg587"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 S/2563: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stanton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-29T10:00:00+08:00">November 29,
                            1941—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 3—6:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1795. Reference Shanghai’s 1646 [<hi rendition="#italic">1746</hi>], November 21,
                    4 p.m. Following the departure of the United States Fourth Marines the Shanghai
                    Provisional Council has assumed responsibility for the <pb facs="0598" n="588"
                        xml:id="pg588"/> maintenance of law and order in Sector C. The Municipal
                    Police have also assumed similar responsibilities in Sector B and have relieved
                    the Shanghai Volunteer Corps who have been on duty in this sector for the past
                    year.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Chungking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
